{"lines": ["One night in 1986, a quiet lake breathed out, and over seventeen hundred people never woke up.", "Lake Nyos, in Cameroon, fills an old volcano, with farming villages in the valleys below.", "For years, gas from hot rock deep underground seeped into the lake bottom through springs.", "But the cold, heavy water down there held it trapped, like soda with the cap on.", "Then, on August twenty-first, something popped that cap, maybe a landslide, maybe cold rain.", "The lake erupted, throwing up a fountain of water and foam a hundred metres high.", "Out came an invisible cloud of carbon dioxide, heavier than air, so it poured down the valleys.", "It moved faster than most people can run, reaching villages twenty-five kilometres away.", "Most victims simply stopped breathing in their sleep.", "When morning came, survivor Joseph Nkwain woke on his floor. His daughter was dead, and so were his neighbours.", "Riding his motorcycle through Nyos, he saw no sign of any living thing.", "Even the lake had turned from blue to deep red, stained by iron from the bottom.", "Today, pipes vent the gas slowly, because those springs are still filling it.", "Would you sleep in a valley below a lake that is still breathing?"], "words": [["One", 0.0, 0.12], ["night", 0.12, 0.36], ["in", 0.36, 0.52], ["1986,", 0.52, 1.3], ["a", 2.0, 2.08], ["quiet", 2.08, 2.36], ["lake", 2.36, 2.76], ["breathed", 2.76, 3.02], ["out,", 3.02, 3.46], ["and", 3.86, 4.06], ["over", 4.06, 4.22], ["seventeen", 4.22, 4.49], ["hundred", 4.49, 4.7], ["people", 4.7, 5.36], ["never", 5.36, 5.64], ["woke", 5.64, 5.92], ["up.", 5.92, 6.22], ["Lake", 6.838, 6.94], ["Nyos,", 6.94, 7.46], ["in", 7.46, 7.64], ["Cameroon,", 7.64, 8.0], ["fills", 8.0, 8.7], ["an", 8.7, 8.96], ["old", 8.96, 9.12], ["volcano,", 9.12, 9.56], ["with", 10.05, 10.32], ["farming", 10.32, 10.68], ["villages", 10.68, 11.06], ["in", 11.06, 11.5], ["the", 11.5, 11.58], ["valleys", 11.58, 11.84], ["below.", 11.84, 12.26], ["For", 12.823, 12.9], 